@WebApplication2_HostAddress = http://localhost:5110

### =========================================================
### DEMO SCRIPT — walk through in this order.
### Story: create staff, book an appointment, diagnose, treat.
### =========================================================


### 1. Create a doctor
# Person + Doctor are created together in one request (shared-key pattern)
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Doctors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dr. John Siddique",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-05-15",
  "contactNumber": "+1-555-1235",
  "speciality": "Cardiology"
}


### 2. Create a patient
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Amira Chen",
  "dateOfBirth": "1998-02-20",
  "contactNumber": "+1-555-9981",
  "medicalHistoryNotes": "No known allergies."
}


### 3. Create a nurse
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Nurses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Priya Nair",
  "dateOfBirth": "1992-11-03",
  "contactNumber": "+1-555-2244",
  "department": "Cardiology Ward"
}


### 4. Confirm all three exist and note their IDs (personId) from the responses above
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Doctors

### 
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Patients

###
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Nurses


### 5. Give the doctor a schedule slot
# Replace doctorId with the personId from step 1
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Schedules
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doctorId": 1,
  "date": "2026-08-01",
  "startTime": "09:00:00",
  "endTime": "17:00:00"
}


### 7. Fetch the appointment back - shows the nested Patient/Doctor/Person data
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments/

### 6. Book an appointment (patient + doctor)
# Replace patientId / doctorId with the personIds from steps 1-2
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 21,
  "doctorId": 34,
  "scheduledTime": "2026-08-01T10:00:00Z"
}


### 7. Fetch the appointment back - shows the nested Patient/Doctor/Person data
# Replace {id} with the id returned by step 6
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments/1


### 8. Try booking with a doctor that doesn't exist - shows validation working
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 2,
  "doctorId": 9999,
  "scheduledTime": "2026-08-01T11:00:00Z"
}
# Expect: 400 Bad Request, "DoctorId does not exist."


### 9. Add a diagnosis for the appointment
# Replace appointmentId with the id from step 6
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Diagnoses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appointmentId": 1,
  "description": "Mild arrhythmia, recommend follow-up ECG.",
  "date": "2026-08-01"
}


### 10. Try adding a second diagnosis to the same appointment - shows one-to-one being enforced
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Diagnoses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appointmentId": 1,
  "description": "Duplicate diagnosis attempt",
  "date": "2026-08-01"
}
# Expect: 409 Conflict, "This appointment already has a diagnosis."


### 11. Add a treatment plan under that diagnosis
# Replace diagnosisId with the id from step 9
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/TreatmentPlans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "diagnosisId": 1,
  "description": "Beta-blocker course, low dose.",
  "duration": "4 weeks"
}


### 12. Log a general medical record note (separate from the formal diagnosis)
POST {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/MedicalRecords
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "patientId": 2,
  "doctorId": 1,
  "notes": "Patient reports occasional palpitations, no chest pain."
}


### 13. Update - change the doctor's speciality
# Replace {id} with the doctor's personId
PUT {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Doctors/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "speciality": "Interventional Cardiology"
}


### 14. Update - patient's medical history notes
PUT {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Patients/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "medicalHistoryNotes": "No known allergies. Follow-up ECG scheduled."
}


### 15. Cancel the appointment (status transition, not a delete)
PATCH {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments/1/cancel


### 16. Confirm the cancellation
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Appointments/1
# Expect: status is now "Cancelled"


### 17. Delete - remove the schedule slot (doctor no longer available that day)
DELETE {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Schedules/1


### 18. Full picture - list everything at the end
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/MedicalRecords

###
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/Diagnoses

###
GET {{WebApplication2_HostAddress}}/api/TreatmentPlans
